    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is >10% above recent 7-day average, reduce by 1–2% per day until convergence.",
    "Increase downward bias when sentiment is positive (≥ 0.50) to counteract overconfidence-driven overestimation.",
    "For 30-day horizons, reduce forecast variance when sentiment is stable (≤ 0.25) to reflect reduced market noise.",
    "If true outcome consistently underperforms forecast (e.g., 3–5 consecutive days), apply a 2–3% downward correction to avoid overoptimism."
